            The best heated vest is the one whose battery you will actually have charged when the snow starts. For Milwaukee M12 owners, that is the M12 Heated AXIS Vest; for DeWalt and Makita owners, their own platform vests. Everyone else should start with the Ororo 4-zone puffer, or the Venustas 20-hour vest for the longest days.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Wear it over a thin base layer, under a windproof coat, start on low when you are working hard, and buy a second battery. That last step does more for warmth than any extra heat zone.
          </p>
